{
  "id": "azure-oidc-subject-mismatch",
  "title": "Azure OIDC login fails after the deploy job moved into a GitHub environment",
  "description": "Squash-merged PR #231 adds `environment: production` to the `Deploy to production` job in .github/workflows/deploy.yml (base/ holds the version before the merge) so production deploys need an approval. Once a job references an environment, GitHub issues its OIDC token with subject repo:example-org/payments-api:environment:production instead of repo:example-org/payments-api:ref:refs/heads/main. The only federated credential on the id-payments-api-deploy managed identity (infra/modules/github-oidc.bicep, deployed by the platform team, not this workflow) trusts the ref:refs/heads/main subject, so azure/login fails with AADSTS700213 \"No matching federated identity record found for presented assertion subject\". The log prints the presented subject claim just above the error, and every earlier main run deployed successfully. The right answer is cloud_auth (OIDC federation); configuration is accepted too because a workflow YAML change triggered it. Either fix is valid: add a federated credential for the environment:production subject (the usual one, keeping the approval gate), or drop the environment line. No fixPath is required because the fix may be on the Azure side.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "payments-api"
  },
